    <!-- About -->
    <sys:String x:Key="About.Finding.Body">Scan for Games reads the install records that Steam, Epic Games, GOG, Ubisoft Connect and the Xbox app keep on this PC. It never asks for launcher passwords and never changes launcher files. EA app games and anything Arclight can't detect can be added with Add a Game.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="About.Finding.Heading">Finding games</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="About.Launching.Body">Games start through their own launcher link (for example Steam) or directly from their executable. Arclight never runs games as administrator on its own.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="About.Launching.Heading">Launching</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="About.Library.Body">Arclight keeps your games, notes, tags, collections and playtime in a local database on this computer. Nothing is uploaded and no account is needed.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="About.Library.Heading">Your library, on your PC</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="About.Playtime.Body">Playtime is counted only while Arclight sees the game's own process running — launchers, crash reporters and anti-cheat helpers don't count. Arclight doesn't import or estimate playtime from Steam or other stores.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="About.Playtime.Heading">Playtime</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="About.Title">How Arclight works</sys:String>

